From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - BinTools_ShapeReader refuses a position reference that leaves the
 stream, loops, or names the wrong kind of record

BinTools_ShapeReader reads a shape, location, curve, surface, polygon or triangulation either
inline or from a position earlier in the file (BinTools_IStream::ReadReference, then GoTo). The
position is trusted, and so is the byte after it:
 - ReadReference returns `position - delta - 1` in unsigned arithmetic. A delta past the start of
   the stream wraps to a position near 2^64, GoTo fails the stream, and the reader goes on reading
   end-of-file bytes as if they were a record.
 - A reference to a shape or a location that is still being read is not found in the position
   table (the entry is written when the record ends), so the reader reads that record again, from
   inside itself: a reference from a compound to the compound that holds it recurses until the stack
   ends. A chain of references to references recurses once per link.
 - A reference to a record that is a null shape (EmptyShape, EndShape) returned a null shape that
   the caller took for the end of its list, and the reference then took its location and its
   orientation.
 - The byte after a shape reference is the orientation, and was cast to TopAbs_Orientation
   without a range check, so a shape with the orientation 255 reached TopAbs::Compose (a table
   lookup) in TopoDS_Iterator and TopExp_Explorer. The continuity byte of an edge was cast to
   GeomAbs_Shape the same way.
 - A location slot that holds some other record type was read as the identity, without consuming
   anything, and a curve, curve 2d, surface, polygon, polygon on triangulation or triangulation
   slot that holds the wrong kind of record was read as a null, so a damaged byte kept the rest of
   the file in step and the reader returned a shape whose structure no longer matched what the
   writer wrote (BRepCheck_Analyzer then faulted on it, #3490).

One rule: a reference names the start of a record before itself, in the stream, that is not a
reference and is not being read, and a type or enumeration byte is one the slot can hold.
BinTools_IStream::ReadReference refuses a delta of zero or one that reaches past the start of the
stream. BinTools_ShapeReader keeps the positions of the shapes and locations it is reading
(a member, myActivePos, cleared by Clear) and refuses a reference to one of them, a reference
whose target is outside the stream or is another reference, and a reference to a null shape. The
orientation and continuity bytes are checked against their enumerations, a location slot against
the four location record types, and each other slot against its record type and the type for a
null. A file the writer wrote is read as before: it never references a reference, a record it is
inside, or a position that holds no record, and it writes only valid bytes.

Failure is Standard_Failure, which is how the reader already reports a damaged record and what the
bridge catches.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3495, follow-up to #3490 and carried patch 0074.

---
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_IStream.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_IStream.cxx
index a838a270a0..8c2f3649bb 100644
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_IStream.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_IStream.cxx
@@ -85,7 +85,9 @@ uint64_t BinTools_IStream::ReadReference()
     default:
       break;
   }
-  if (aDelta == 0)
+  // a reference names a record before itself: a delta of zero, or one that reaches past the start
+  // of the stream, is damage, and the unsigned subtraction below would wrap to a huge position
+  if (aDelta == 0 || aDelta >= aCurrentPos)
   {
     Standard_SStream aMsg;
     aMsg << "BinTools_IStream::ReadReference: invalid reference " << (char)myLastType << '\n';
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_ShapeReader.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_ShapeReader.cxx
index f6aa27e1dd..ba396ab31f 100644
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_ShapeReader.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_ShapeReader.cxx
@@ -42,6 +42,64 @@ static bool IsPolygonOfTriangulation(const occ::handle<Poly_PolygonOnTriangulati
   return true;
 }
 
+namespace
+{
+//! Forgets the position of a record that is being read when the read ends, by return or by throw.
+class ActivePosition
+{
+public:
+  ActivePosition(NCollection_Map<uint64_t>& theMap, const uint64_t thePosition)
+      : myMap(theMap),
+        myPosition(thePosition)
+  {
+    myMap.Add(thePosition);
+  }
+
+  ~ActivePosition() { myMap.Remove(myPosition); }
+
+  ActivePosition(const ActivePosition&)            = delete;
+  ActivePosition& operator=(const ActivePosition&) = delete;
+
+private:
+  NCollection_Map<uint64_t>& myMap;
+  uint64_t                   myPosition;
+};
+
+//! Moves to the record a reference names. The writer references the start of a record it has
+//! written, so the target is inside the stream, is not a reference itself (a chain of references
+//! recurses once per link) and is not a record that is still being read (a cycle recurses
+//! without end).
+void GoToReferenced(BinTools_IStream&                theStream,
+                    const uint64_t                   theRef,
+                    const NCollection_Map<uint64_t>& theActive)
+{
+  if (theActive.Contains(theRef))
+  {
+    throw Standard_Failure("BinTools_ShapeReader: a reference to a record that is being read");
+  }
+  theStream.GoTo(theRef);
+  const int aNext = theStream ? theStream.Stream().peek() : EOF;
+  if (aNext == EOF
+      || (aNext >= BinTools_ObjectType_Reference8 && aNext <= BinTools_ObjectType_Reference64))
+  {
+    throw Standard_Failure("BinTools_ShapeReader: a reference to a position that holds no record");
+  }
+}
+
+//! A byte read as a TopAbs_Orientation or a GeomAbs_Shape that the enumeration does not have.
+uint8_t ReadEnumByte(BinTools_IStream& theStream, const uint8_t theMax, const char* theName)
+{
+  const uint8_t aByte = theStream.ReadByte();
+  if (aByte > theMax)
+  {
+    Standard_SStream aMsg;
+    aMsg << "BinTools_ShapeReader: " << theName << " out of range: " << int(aByte) << '\n';
+    throw Standard_Failure(aMsg.str().c_str());
+  }
+  return aByte;
+}
+} // namespace
+
 //=================================================================================================
 
 BinTools_ShapeReader::BinTools_ShapeReader() = default;
@@ -63,6 +121,7 @@ void BinTools_ShapeReader::Clear()
   myPolygon3dPos.Clear();
   myPolygonPos.Clear();
   myTriangulationPos.Clear();
+  myActivePos.Clear();
 }
 
 //=================================================================================================
@@ -96,14 +155,20 @@ TopoDS_Shape BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadShape(BinTools_IStream& theStream)
     else
     {
       uint64_t aCurrent = theStream.Position();
-      theStream.GoTo(aRef); // go to the referenced position
+      GoToReferenced(theStream, aRef, myActivePos); // go to the referenced position
       aResult = ReadShape(theStream);
       theStream.GoTo(aCurrent); // returns to the current position
     }
+    if (aResult.IsNull())
+    {
+      throw Standard_Failure("BinTools_ShapeReader: a reference to a null shape");
+    }
     aResult.Location(*ReadLocation(theStream), false);
-    aResult.Orientation(TopAbs_Orientation(theStream.ReadByte()));
+    aResult.Orientation(
+      TopAbs_Orientation(ReadEnumByte(theStream, TopAbs_EXTERNAL, "orientation")));
     return aResult;
   }
+  ActivePosition aActive(myActivePos, aPosition);
   // read the shape
   TopAbs_ShapeEnum       aShapeType        = theStream.ShapeType();
   TopAbs_Orientation     aShapeOrientation = theStream.ShapeOrientation();
@@ -219,7 +284,7 @@ TopoDS_Shape BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadShape(BinTools_IStream& theStream)
               if (aClosed)
               {
                 aCurve2d_2 = ReadCurve2d(theStream);
-                aReg       = (GeomAbs_Shape)theStream.ReadByte();
+                aReg       = (GeomAbs_Shape)ReadEnumByte(theStream, GeomAbs_CN, "continuity");
               }
               occ::handle<Geom_Surface> aSurface = ReadSurface(theStream);
               const TopLoc_Location*    aLoc     = ReadLocation(theStream);
@@ -243,7 +308,7 @@ TopoDS_Shape BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadShape(BinTools_IStream& theStream)
             }
             case 4: // -4- Regularity
             {
-              GeomAbs_Shape             aReg      = (GeomAbs_Shape)theStream.ReadByte();
+              GeomAbs_Shape aReg = (GeomAbs_Shape)ReadEnumByte(theStream, GeomAbs_CN, "continuity");
               occ::handle<Geom_Surface> aSurface1 = ReadSurface(theStream);
               const TopLoc_Location*    aLoc1     = ReadLocation(theStream);
               occ::handle<Geom_Surface> aSurface2 = ReadSurface(theStream);
@@ -384,12 +449,17 @@ const TopLoc_Location* BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadLocation(BinTools_IStream& theS
       return aFound;
     }
     uint64_t aCurrent = theStream.Position();
-    theStream.GoTo(aRef); // go to the referenced position
+    GoToReferenced(theStream, aRef, myActivePos); // go to the referenced position
     const TopLoc_Location* aResult = ReadLocation(theStream);
     theStream.GoTo(aCurrent); // returns to the current position
     return aResult;
   }
-  // read the location directly from the stream
+  // read the location directly from the stream; any other type is a record of another kind
+  if (aType != BinTools_ObjectType_SimpleLocation && aType != BinTools_ObjectType_Location)
+  {
+    throw Standard_Failure("BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadLocation: unexpected record type");
+  }
+  ActivePosition  aActive(myActivePos, aPosition);
   TopLoc_Location aLoc;
   if (aType == BinTools_ObjectType_SimpleLocation)
   {
@@ -431,7 +501,7 @@ occ::handle<Geom_Curve> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadCurve(BinTools_IStream& theStr
       return *aFound;
     }
     uint64_t aCurrent = theStream.Position();
-    theStream.GoTo(aRef); // go to the referenced position
+    GoToReferenced(theStream, aRef, myActivePos); // go to the referenced position
     aResult = ReadCurve(theStream);
     theStream.GoTo(aCurrent); // returns to the current position
   }
@@ -441,6 +511,10 @@ occ::handle<Geom_Curve> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadCurve(BinTools_IStream& theStr
     theStream.UpdatePosition();
     myCurvePos.Bind(aPosition, aResult);
   }
+  else if (theStream.LastType() != BinTools_ObjectType_EmptyCurve)
+  {
+    throw Standard_Failure("BinTools_ShapeReader: unexpected record type, expected a Curve");
+  }
   return aResult;
 }
 
@@ -460,7 +534,7 @@ occ::handle<Geom2d_Curve> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadCurve2d(BinTools_IStream& th
       return *aFound;
     }
     uint64_t aCurrent = theStream.Position();
-    theStream.GoTo(aRef); // go to the referenced position
+    GoToReferenced(theStream, aRef, myActivePos); // go to the referenced position
     aResult = ReadCurve2d(theStream);
     theStream.GoTo(aCurrent); // returns to the current position
   }
@@ -470,6 +544,10 @@ occ::handle<Geom2d_Curve> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadCurve2d(BinTools_IStream& th
     theStream.UpdatePosition();
     myCurve2dPos.Bind(aPosition, aResult);
   }
+  else if (theStream.LastType() != BinTools_ObjectType_EmptyCurve2d)
+  {
+    throw Standard_Failure("BinTools_ShapeReader: unexpected record type, expected a Curve2d");
+  }
   return aResult;
 }
 
@@ -489,7 +567,7 @@ occ::handle<Geom_Surface> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadSurface(BinTools_IStream& th
       return *aFound;
     }
     uint64_t aCurrent = theStream.Position();
-    theStream.GoTo(aRef); // go to the referenced position
+    GoToReferenced(theStream, aRef, myActivePos); // go to the referenced position
     aResult = ReadSurface(theStream);
     theStream.GoTo(aCurrent); // returns to the current position
   }
@@ -499,6 +577,10 @@ occ::handle<Geom_Surface> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadSurface(BinTools_IStream& th
     theStream.UpdatePosition();
     mySurfacePos.Bind(aPosition, aResult);
   }
+  else if (theStream.LastType() != BinTools_ObjectType_EmptySurface)
+  {
+    throw Standard_Failure("BinTools_ShapeReader: unexpected record type, expected a Surface");
+  }
   return aResult;
 }
 
@@ -518,7 +600,7 @@ occ::handle<Poly_Polygon3D> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadPolygon3d(BinTools_IStream
       return *aFound;
     }
     uint64_t aCurrent = theStream.Position();
-    theStream.GoTo(aRef); // go to the referenced position
+    GoToReferenced(theStream, aRef, myActivePos); // go to the referenced position
     aResult = ReadPolygon3d(theStream);
     theStream.GoTo(aCurrent); // returns to the current position
   }
@@ -549,6 +631,10 @@ occ::handle<Poly_Polygon3D> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadPolygon3d(BinTools_IStream
     }
     myPolygon3dPos.Bind(aPosition, aResult);
   }
+  else if (theStream.LastType() != BinTools_ObjectType_EmptyPolygon3d)
+  {
+    throw Standard_Failure("BinTools_ShapeReader: unexpected record type, expected a Polygon3d");
+  }
   return aResult;
 }
 
@@ -569,7 +655,7 @@ occ::handle<Poly_PolygonOnTriangulation> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadPolygon(
       return *aFound;
     }
     uint64_t aCurrent = theStream.Position();
-    theStream.GoTo(aRef); // go to the referenced position
+    GoToReferenced(theStream, aRef, myActivePos); // go to the referenced position
     aResult = ReadPolygon(theStream);
     theStream.GoTo(aCurrent); // returns to the current position
   }
@@ -599,6 +685,11 @@ occ::handle<Poly_PolygonOnTriangulation> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadPolygon(
     }
     myPolygonPos.Bind(aPosition, aResult);
   }
+  else if (theStream.LastType() != BinTools_ObjectType_EmptyPolygonOnTriangulation)
+  {
+    throw Standard_Failure(
+      "BinTools_ShapeReader: unexpected record type, expected a PolygonOnTriangulation");
+  }
   return aResult;
 }
 
@@ -618,7 +709,7 @@ occ::handle<Poly_Triangulation> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadTriangulation(BinTools
       return *aFound;
     }
     uint64_t aCurrent = theStream.Position();
-    theStream.GoTo(aRef); // go to the referenced position
+    GoToReferenced(theStream, aRef, myActivePos); // go to the referenced position
     aResult = ReadTriangulation(theStream);
     theStream.GoTo(aCurrent); // returns to the current position
   }
@@ -681,5 +772,10 @@ occ::handle<Poly_Triangulation> BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadTriangulation(BinTools
 
     myTriangulationPos.Bind(aPosition, aResult);
   }
+  else if (aType != BinTools_ObjectType_EmptyTriangulation)
